1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:04,170
Department settings change how a whole
department sees and handles its work.

2
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:07,289
They deserve the same review as a dispatch
procedure.

3
00:00:07,769 --> 00:00:10,789
Open the department menu, then Department
Settings.

4
00:00:11,279 --> 00:00:14,930
We are using the fictional Firehouse
fifty-one department, but these

5
00:00:14,930 --> 00:00:18,649
controls are equally relevant to a mobile
crisis service, a search

6
00:00:18,649 --> 00:00:23,549
team, a patrol company, a wildland
contractor, or a plant response team.

7
00:00:24,059 --> 00:00:26,610
Begin by identifying the problem you want
to solve.

8
00:00:27,129 --> 00:00:29,370
Is the roster showing stale availability?

9
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:32,549
Are off-duty members receiving unwanted
alerts?

10
00:00:33,009 --> 00:00:35,580
Is a module confusing members who do not
use it?

11
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:40,209
Make one deliberate change, save it, and
check its effect before

12
00:00:40,209 --> 00:00:42,240
changing several related controls.

13
00:00:42,439 --> 00:00:45,179
The department name identifies this
workspace.

14
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:49,539
The time zone affects local time displays
and scheduled work; our

15
00:00:49,539 --> 00:00:51,500
training department uses Central Time.

16
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:56,099
Use twenty-four-hour time changes how
supported screens display the clock.

17
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:59,350
It does not create twenty-four-hour
staffing coverage.

18
00:00:59,750 --> 00:01:03,729
Account Owner identifies the managing
account; review ownership

19
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:07,309
and administrative access in the personnel
and security workflows.

20
00:01:07,789 --> 00:01:11,510
Disable Auto-Available controls the
automatic behavior described

21
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:15,740
on this screen: setting personnel status
to Available after an hour.

22
00:01:16,129 --> 00:01:19,170
In this lesson we turn that automatic
behavior off.

23
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:22,819
This avoids treating the passage of time
as evidence that a person

24
00:01:22,819 --> 00:01:24,409
has finished a long assignment.

25
00:01:24,789 --> 00:01:29,129
It also makes deliberate member updates
and supervisor follow-up more important.

26
00:01:29,559 --> 00:01:32,679
Saving the setting is separate from
proving the worker’s behavior

27
00:01:32,679 --> 00:01:37,240
over time; this recording verifies the
saved configuration, not a

28
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:39,140
one-hour background-worker test.

29
00:01:39,309 --> 00:01:43,149
Modern notifications selects supported
modern notification behavior,

30
00:01:43,339 --> 00:01:44,999
including modern push sounds.

31
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:49,380
It does not establish a valid device
registration or prove delivery.

32
00:01:49,809 --> 00:01:52,950
Review every channel and consumer your
department uses.

33
00:01:53,370 --> 00:01:57,659
Require password resets by email directs
administrator-initiated member

34
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:01,609
resets through single-use recovery links
instead of an administrator

35
00:02:01,609 --> 00:02:03,150
selecting a member’s password.

36
00:02:03,609 --> 00:02:08,159
Require Security PIN governs sensitive
supported assistant and text actions.

37
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:11,449
These are security decisions, and the
owning administrator

38
00:02:11,449 --> 00:02:14,660
needs to review recovery arrangements and
member enrollment.

39
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:18,320
We leave their existing values visible and
discuss their impact

40
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:19,820
without changing credentials.

41
00:02:20,219 --> 00:02:23,710
T T S Language selects the application’s
voice-prompt language.

42
00:02:24,030 --> 00:02:26,820
That setting is separate from the Warm
Lulu narration

43
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:28,169
used in this training video.

44
00:02:28,349 --> 00:02:31,520
Under Sorting, we choose LastName for
personnel.

45
00:02:31,970 --> 00:02:34,359
Units and calls have their own order
settings.

46
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:37,809
This is useful when a dispatcher knows the
member’s surname and

47
00:02:37,809 --> 00:02:39,290
needs a predictable roster.

48
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:43,009
The Address section describes the
department base or office.

49
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:44,830
Our address is fictional.

50
00:02:45,299 --> 00:02:48,639
Default Map Center accepts decimal
latitude and longitude.

51
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:53,570
Explicit coordinates pin the starting
point; leaving both blank lets the system

52
00:02:53,570 --> 00:02:55,619
work out a center from the saved address.

53
00:02:56,090 --> 00:02:59,600
A department center is a map starting
point, not a live unit

54
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:03,540
location, a patrol boundary, or proof that
a resource is present.

55
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,880
A search team can use its base, a security
company its operational office, and an

56
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:11,410
industrial team its facility access point.

57
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:15,579
For a contractor deployment, review
whether the department center or an

58
00:03:15,579 --> 00:03:17,599
incident-specific view is appropriate.

59
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:22,359
Personnel Staffing Reset and Personnel
Status Reset are different controls.

60
00:03:22,809 --> 00:03:27,379
Staffing describes availability; status
describes current activity.

61
00:03:27,930 --> 00:03:31,699
Our example enables the daily staffing
reset at eight a m and

62
00:03:31,699 --> 00:03:33,819
selects Unavailable as its target.

63
00:03:34,319 --> 00:03:37,710
Members then need to declare their
availability after the reset.

64
00:03:38,159 --> 00:03:41,360
This can help a volunteer search
department avoid relying on

65
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:46,120
yesterday’s availability, or a wildland
contractor require a fresh crew check.

66
00:03:46,479 --> 00:03:49,770
It can also disrupt a team working
overnight if the time and

67
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:51,779
target do not fit its procedures.

68
00:03:52,209 --> 00:03:55,180
The daily status reset remains off in this
example.

69
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:59,950
Consider extended searches, patrol
assignments, mental health responses

70
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:04,360
and plant incidents before automatically
replacing a current activity status.

71
00:04:04,799 --> 00:04:08,889
When you create custom personnel staffing
or status sets, revisit these

72
00:04:08,889 --> 00:04:13,270
target selections; the intended label must
resolve to the current option.

73
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:16,969
The staffing suppression section lets the
department select staffing

74
00:04:16,969 --> 00:04:20,349
levels that should be muted by supported
notification paths.

75
00:04:20,729 --> 00:04:23,460
We enable suppression and select
Unavailable.

76
00:04:23,979 --> 00:04:27,990
Review the interaction carefully: at the
daily reset, members are

77
00:04:27,990 --> 00:04:31,730
marked Unavailable, and supported
notifications can suppress them

78
00:04:31,759 --> 00:04:33,360
until their staffing is updated.

79
00:04:33,749 --> 00:04:38,419
This reduces off-duty noise, but a stale
staffing declaration can exclude

80
00:04:38,419 --> 00:04:40,149
the person you intended to reach.

81
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:43,509
For security, the procedure might
distinguish on-duty

82
00:04:43,509 --> 00:04:45,349
patrol from off-duty staff.

83
00:04:45,710 --> 00:04:49,000
A mobile response service might
distinguish the scheduled response

84
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,579
team from the broader roster.

85
00:04:50,930 --> 00:04:55,430
An industrial team might distinguish the
current plant E R T from other employees.

86
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:59,020
Verify the intended recipients and
fallback procedures.

87
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:03,940
This isolated training stack does not send
real alerts, so this lesson does

88
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:06,099
not claim an external delivery test.

89
00:05:06,310 --> 00:05:08,870
Click Save, then reopen the settings.

90
00:05:09,349 --> 00:05:14,479
In this build the department form does not
show a useful success banner, so reopening

91
00:05:14,479 --> 00:05:16,290
is an important persistence check.

92
00:05:16,729 --> 00:05:21,290
Our saved values show Disable
Auto-Available checked, LastName sorting,

93
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:26,780
daily staffing reset enabled at eight a m
to Unavailable, daily status reset off,

94
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,110
and suppression enabled for Unavailable.

95
00:05:29,559 --> 00:05:32,510
These are the values actually retained by
the application.

96
00:05:32,979 --> 00:05:36,869
Force Department Update requests a
department cache refresh if clients

97
00:05:36,869 --> 00:05:38,870
retain stale department information.

98
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:42,230
Read its timing notice and allow clients
to refresh or

99
00:05:42,230 --> 00:05:43,850
sign in again where appropriate.

100
00:05:44,339 --> 00:05:47,710
A cache refresh is not a substitute for
saving a form or

101
00:05:47,710 --> 00:05:49,320
testing a notification channel.

102
00:05:49,710 --> 00:05:52,740
Investigate the owning screen and saved
value first.

103
00:05:52,950 --> 00:05:54,450
Open Department Modules.

104
00:05:54,850 --> 00:05:58,649
These switches control supported module
availability and navigation.

105
00:05:59,050 --> 00:06:03,319
Turning a module on does not purchase its
add-on, grant missing permissions,

106
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:05,489
or configure an external provider.

107
00:06:05,909 --> 00:06:08,020
We turn Calendar off and save.

108
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:11,539
The page confirms the module settings were
saved, and Calendar

109
00:06:11,539 --> 00:06:13,070
disappears from the side menu.

110
00:06:13,670 --> 00:06:17,029
We then turn Calendar back on, save, and
reopen it.

111
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:20,160
The three original training events are
still present.

112
00:06:20,459 --> 00:06:23,230
Disabling the module did not delete those
records.

113
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:26,710
The screen also warns that propagation can
differ across

114
00:06:26,710 --> 00:06:30,699
features, so review the screens and apps
your department actually uses.

115
00:06:31,190 --> 00:06:35,630
For your practice exercise, select one
behavior, explain who it affects,

116
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:39,530
save it in a training department, reopen
it and inspect the result.

117
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:44,089
Document the responsible reviewer and an
operational test for any effect

118
00:06:44,089 --> 00:06:46,170
this configuration check cannot prove.

